# Generated by XcodeGen — regenerate with `xcodegen generate`.
# The Info.plist and .entitlements files are written from the `info:` and
# `entitlements:` blocks in project.yml, which is the reviewable source of truth.
#
# The .xcodeproj is committed anyway: Xcode Cloud builds straight from the
# checkout and never runs XcodeGen. Everything inside it is ignored except the
# two files that build needs — the project itself and the resolved SwiftPM
# graph. Without the latter, Xcode falls back to CribWireKit/Package.resolved,
# which pins only the kit's own dependencies and knows nothing of WebRTC or the
# Tidal SDK, and resolution fails outright because Xcode Cloud disables
# automatic dependency resolution. Re-run `xcodebuild -resolvePackageDependencies`
# and commit the updated Package.resolved whenever `packages:` in project.yml
# changes.
CribWire.xcodeproj/*
!CribWire.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
!CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/
CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/*
!CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/
CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/*
!CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/
CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/*
!CribWire.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/Package.resolved

# The umbrella workspace is generated too, and holds nothing reviewable.
/CribWire.xcworkspace/
CribWire/Info.plist
CribWire/CribWire.entitlements
CribWireWidgets/Info.plist

# SwiftPM
.build/
.swiftpm/

# Xcode
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
